Owners' Fund
Main Features of Owners' Fund
Provision of Risk Capital: The owners' fund is also known
as the risk capital of the business, as the return on this
capital depends upon the rate of earning of the
company. In case company is incurring loss then it is not
compulsory to pay any return on owners' fund. If loss
continues, owners may be unable to recover even their
original investment. In times of prosperity high level of
return is given on owners' fund. The return on owners'
fund varies with the profit earning of the company,
that is why, it is called risky capital.
